+   * digit wide, so before 10 o'clock the string begins with an invisible
+   * digit-sized gap. Centring the label centres that gap too and pushes the
+   * visible time half a digit right; the date, which has no padding, sat
+   * correctly and made the clock look like the broken one. g_strstrip does not
+   * help here - it only knows ASCII whitespace. */
+  trimmed = luma_trim_clock (time);
